1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:01,918
[BEA] <i>Ma…</i>

2
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:04,004
<i>Please, don't do that again.</i>

3
00:00:04,087 --> 00:00:06,923
<i>Remember what I told you? I'll find a way.</i>

4
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:09,592
<i>I promise you.</i>
<i>I'll get back at Billy.</i>

5
00:00:09,676 --> 00:00:11,219
[BILLY] <i>They may be delusional.</i>

6
00:00:11,302 --> 00:00:14,431
<i>They believe in</i>
<i>their own version of the truth.</i>

7
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:16,766
<i>Bea has to pay for what she did.</i>

8
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:17,767
<i>- I told you--</i>
<i>- Well?</i>

9
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:19,227
<i>You still haven't found my grandpa?!</i>

10
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:20,937
[MAN] <i>Sir, we're very, very sorry.</i>

11
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:23,273
<i>But we're still looking for him.</i>
<i>We are looking for him, sir.</i>

12
00:00:24,774 --> 00:00:25,859
<i>Jordan!</i>

13
00:00:25,942 --> 00:00:28,319
<i>Dude, I can't find him!</i>

14
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:30,739
<i>Please, I can't lose him too.</i>

15
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:32,532
<i>Jordan, breathe. Breathe.</i>

16
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:34,951
<i>Let's split up so we can find him faster.</i>

17
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,537
<i>I'll go this way, you go that way.</i>
<i>Breathe, we'll find him.</i>

18
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,580
<i>- Thank you.</i>
- [WOMAN]<i> Sure.</i>

19
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:40,790
<i>Grandpa! Grandpa Jude!</i>

20
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:43,168
<i>Hi, Grandpa!</i>

21
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:44,419
<i>Are you okay?</i>

22
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:47,630
<i>I saw my son-in-law again.</i>

23
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:51,551
<i>He's not a good husband.</i>

24
00:00:51,634 --> 00:00:53,470
<i>And he's not a good father either.</i>

25
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:56,806
<i>But he's tried to reach out several times.</i>

26
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:58,308
<i>It got me thinking.</i>

27
00:00:59,809 --> 00:01:02,520
<i>What if he came back</i>
<i>because he has changed?</i>

28
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:08,068
<i>Who am I to deny my grandson's right</i>
<i>to see his father?</i>

29
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:11,863
<i>My grandson grew up</i>

30
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:15,825
<i>with hatred for his father.</i>

31
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,327
<i>It's hard to live</i>

32
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:19,370
<i>with resentment in your heart.</i>

33
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:21,623
<i>My parents disowned me when I was a kid.</i>

34
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:24,250
<i>Life was hard because I was alone.</i>

35
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:27,420
<i>But everything changed</i>
<i>when I met this girl.</i>

36
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:29,714
<i>So I'll marry her</i>

37
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:32,217
<i>once I find a way to escape from here.</i>

38
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:33,968
[LAUGHS]

39
00:01:34,552 --> 00:01:35,553
<i>Oliver.</i>

40
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:37,514
<i>You're not going to school.</i>

41
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:38,598
<i>Why?</i>

42
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:40,850
<i>Your sister and I need to make sure</i>

43
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:42,560
<i>that your father</i>
<i>is no longer working there.</i>

44
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:43,728
[OLIVER] <i>I'm going.</i>

45
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:46,105
[PRECIOUS]
<i>Oliver, you're not.</i>

46
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:49,275
<i>Pa?</i>

47
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,072
[OLIVER] <i>Why did you leave us?</i>

48
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:56,866
<i>I made mistakes, son.</i>

49
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,243
<i>I admit it.</i>

50
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,078
<i>I wasn't a good father.</i>

51
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,539
<i>I love you and Billy, both of you.</i>

52
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:05,500
<i>I'd do anything to earn your forgiveness.</i>

53
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,418
[SOBS SOFTLY]

54
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:08,545
<i>Pa…</i>

55
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:11,673
<i>I already forgave you.</i>

56
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:13,925
<i>And besides,</i>

57
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:16,886
<i>I told you, remember?</i>

58
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,888
<i>I'll help you.</i>

59
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:21,391
<i>Billy has a good heart,</i>

60
00:02:21,474 --> 00:02:24,727
<i>even if she can be a tiger sometimes.</i>

61
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:25,770
[CHUCKLING]

62
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:28,523
<i>- You got that from Billy.</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

63
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:31,818
<i>She was the first one</i>
<i>to teach me self-defense.</i>

64
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:33,778
<i>Is that why you punched Biboy?</i>

65
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:35,488
<i>It wasn't just that, Pa.</i>

66
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:37,824
<i>She also talked back to Biboy's dad.</i>

67
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:40,368
<i>She didn't back down at all!</i>

68
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:43,163
<i>Ready to go, Auntie?</i>

69
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:44,747
[ENRICO] <i>Think you can do that?</i>

70
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:47,834
- [OLIVER] <i>Sure I can.</i>
- [ENRICO] <i>Bullseye both times!</i>

71
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:51,838
[OLIVER] <i>Did those two boys cry?</i>
<i>That must've hurt, huh?</i>

72
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:53,882
You're sure about this, Billy?

73
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:56,301
You don't want Oliver to go home for now?

74
00:02:58,469 --> 00:03:00,430
What else can I do, Auntie?

75
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:04,350
He's so stubborn. Such an obstinate kid!

76
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:08,730
Wonder where he got that from?

77
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:14,235
Well, at least he knows
how to fight for what he wants.

78
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:17,989
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

79
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:20,491
He's growing up, Auntie Pres.

80
00:03:21,075 --> 00:03:22,911
He makes his own choices now.

81
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:28,249
You okay with this?

82
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:31,961
For now.

83
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:36,549
Look how happy he was with his dad.

84
00:03:39,135 --> 00:03:41,387
I can't take that away from him, Auntie.

85
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:45,016
[UPLIFTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:03:45,099 --> 00:03:47,268
Billy is really cool.

87
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:49,979
That's why everyone's intimidated by her.

88
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,607
Sometimes, I am too.

89
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:54,400
Only sometimes?

90
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:58,238
- Actually, all the time.
- [BOTH CHUCKLING]

91
00:03:58,321 --> 00:03:59,614
But you know, Pa?

92
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:03,618
When it comes to Auntie,
she folds so fast.

93
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:06,412
[CHUCKLES] Oh, by the way.

94
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:10,875
Your sister and your auntie
should know that you're here.

95
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:12,293
They'll be worried about you for sure.

96
00:04:12,377 --> 00:04:13,628
But, Pa,

97
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:17,340
they'll stop me from meeting up
with you again.

98
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:18,967
You know, Oliver,

99
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,594
you have to understand them.

100
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:25,014
You did nothing wrong.
I'm the one who's to blame here.

101
00:04:26,891 --> 00:04:29,894
So you need to understand
where they're coming from.

102
00:04:29,978 --> 00:04:31,479
Don't be mad at them.

103
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:35,692
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

104
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:37,485
[GROANS]

105
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:38,820
Dear.

106
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:40,154
- Ma.
- Where's your laundry?

107
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,072
I'll do the laundry.

108
00:04:41,155 --> 00:04:43,116
No need. I'll do it myself.

109
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:45,660
Let me do it. Just go to work.

110
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:47,870
And won't you get your paycheck already?

111
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:50,999
I will, Ma. Don't worry.
I'll pester them about it.

112
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:53,710
- I'll get to work then.
- All right. Be careful.

113
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:54,836
I will.

114
00:04:54,919 --> 00:05:01,884
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]
- [UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

115
00:05:05,763 --> 00:05:07,557
[SNIFFLES]

116
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:17,859
[ZIPPER OPENS]

117
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:26,326
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

118
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:44,385
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:27,845
[PHONE RINGING]

120
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,138
Hm?

121
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,974
[RINGING CONTINUES]

122
00:06:33,893 --> 00:06:34,852
Hello?

123
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,688
Sorry, Billy.

124
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:39,232
I ducked out.

125
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:42,902
We know.

126
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:45,530
[BILLY] <i>You're in school, right?</i>

127
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:46,739
Yes.

128
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,783
I went to see Papa.

129
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:51,160
But I'll be going home soon.

130
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:53,955
Auntie Pres and I are here at the school.

131
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,540
Huh?

132
00:06:55,623 --> 00:06:59,460
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

133
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:03,881
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,591
[PHONE RINGING]

135
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:07,718
[GASPS] Really, Dad? For me?

136
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:10,179
Yes, that is my graduation gift for you!

137
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:11,764
- Thank you, Daddy!
- Happy?

138
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:14,016
- Of course!
- Let's go eat!

139
00:07:15,059 --> 00:07:16,727
[CUSTOMER] Miss!

140
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:19,397
Miss, I bought this from you yesterday.

141
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:20,982
It's so slow. Why is that?

142
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:23,192
Hey, miss!

143
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:25,903
Miss, I'm talking to you! Hello?

144
00:07:26,904 --> 00:07:28,739
- [CUSTOMER] What's the deal?
- Are you in a rush, huh?

145
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:31,576
Can't you wait? Is there
a taxi waiting for you?

146
00:07:31,659 --> 00:07:35,371
- [GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [PHONE BUSY TONE]

147
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:38,040
[SNIFFLING]

148
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:44,046
- [PHONE BUSY TONE]
- What's with this thing?

149
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,591
Look. The battery drains so fast.

150
00:07:46,674 --> 00:07:50,511
I installed one app and look, it froze!

151
00:07:50,595 --> 00:07:51,596
What's up?

152
00:07:51,679 --> 00:07:52,555
- Look.
- Miss.

153
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:55,516
Maybe the problem is with
the app you installed.

154
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:58,144
This phone is brand new.

155
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:04,442
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

156
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:07,737
[PHONE BUSY TONE]

157
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,197
[SCREAMS]

158
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:14,577
[SOBBING]

159
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:30,885
[SCREAMING AND WAILING]

160
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:34,889
[PHONE CLATTERING]

161
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:38,059
The phone isn't the problem!
You know what the problem is?!

162
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:40,102
That annoying app!

163
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:42,104
My goodness…

164
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:47,985
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

165
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:54,158
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

166
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,451
[SLAMS COUNTER]

167
00:08:57,161 --> 00:08:58,579
Billy, Auntie.

168
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:00,957
[BILLY] Hm.

169
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:03,709
[SOFTLY] Auntie…

170
00:09:05,127 --> 00:09:08,673
Billy, I'm sorry for leaving
without letting you know.

171
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,092
We got so worried.

172
00:09:11,175 --> 00:09:12,635
Don't do it again, okay?

173
00:09:12,718 --> 00:09:14,178
Okay, Auntie.

174
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:16,138
Billy, can I--

175
00:09:16,222 --> 00:09:17,640
Let's talk at home.

176
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:19,767
So I don't have to go home yet?

177
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,895
Yeah, you can still make it
to your next class.

178
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,772
Here are your things.

179
00:09:24,855 --> 00:09:26,649
Go on then.

180
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:29,819
Bye-bye, Billy, Auntie!

181
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:33,489
I'll see him off.

182
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:39,787
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:50,047
[ENGINE STARTS]

184
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:10,109
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:22,747
So when Mr. Fabrizio arrives,

186
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:26,500
he'll ask us if we're ready
for a global rollout for sure.

187
00:10:27,251 --> 00:10:28,878
We're more than ready.

188
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:31,380
- The servers are already multi-regional.
- [WHISPERS] Okay.

189
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:34,967
Even if the users overseas
sign up all at the same time,

190
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,177
we're on par.

191
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:37,136
Good.

192
00:10:37,219 --> 00:10:39,639
I'm sure he'll ask you,

193
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:42,099
"What makes LoveList different

194
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:43,976
from the other swiping apps?"

195
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,645
[CLICKS FINGERS]

196
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:47,104
Hmm…

197
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:48,981
- Well…
- [BILLY] Mm-hmm.

198
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:50,399
We're not just swipe-based.

199
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:53,444
Our matching engine is behavior-driven.

200
00:10:53,527 --> 00:10:54,612
Mm-hmm.

201
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:58,240
It learns from conversations,
activity patterns,

202
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:00,117
as well as response timing.

203
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:02,995
So as people use the app,

204
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:04,872
the matches become more accurate.

205
00:11:04,955 --> 00:11:06,457
Very good.

206
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:08,084
That's exactly what he needs to hear.

207
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:09,168
Yes, boss.

208
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:10,461
[PHONE CHIMES]

209
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:14,048
Okay.

210
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:15,007
Here we go.

211
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:17,510
- He's arriving in 15 minutes.
- [CLEARS THROAT]

212
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:19,095
[BILLY] Whoo.

213
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,846
[BILLY EXHALES]

214
00:11:22,598 --> 00:11:24,016
[HUFFS]

215
00:11:25,976 --> 00:11:26,811
What?

216
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,146
Do I have something on my face?

217
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:30,481
- What?
- It's not that.

218
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:32,358
I'm just thinking…

219
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:34,777
How do you do that?

220
00:11:37,029 --> 00:11:39,156
Like, compartmentalizing.

221
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:42,451
So easy to just turn off a problem,

222
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:43,994
focus on another…

223
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:46,997
It's like you don't even think about…

224
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:48,916
About what?

225
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:51,752
About Oliver.

226
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:52,795
Hmm.

227
00:11:53,838 --> 00:11:56,757
That he's already talking to your father.

228
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,677
I just didn't expect that

229
00:12:00,344 --> 00:12:01,637
you'd let him.

230
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:05,349
You know, I just gave Oliver what--

231
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:06,809
What he wanted?

232
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:10,312
What he needed.

233
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:16,819
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

234
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:23,617
I kept it a secret from him for years.

235
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:27,663
Because I wanted to protect him.

236
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:30,583
But you know, dude,

237
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:34,211
when I saw him with that man,

238
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:37,673
I felt guilty.

239
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:42,636
So no matter how angry I was at him,

240
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:47,808
I knew I was wrong to decide for Oliver.

241
00:12:48,893 --> 00:12:51,562
It was wrong for me
to make decisions for him.

242
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,734
Because all he wants is to know his dad.

243
00:12:56,817 --> 00:13:02,364
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

244
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:04,950
Dude, are you convinced that

245
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:07,828
your dad is truly remorseful?

246
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:10,289
This isn't about him anymore, dude.

247
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:14,502
This is all about Oliver now.

248
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:20,925
Okay.

249
00:13:22,551 --> 00:13:24,637
So, what's your plan?

250
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:32,269
Get out of here!
I'll take care of things here.

251
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:50,746
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

252
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:51,830
Mr. Dino.

253
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,415
Good morning.

254
00:13:54,959 --> 00:13:56,877
Why'd you choose to join our group?

255
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,922
I just wanted to talk to you guys.

256
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:01,757
I just wanted to share.

257
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:04,552
My officer said…

258
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:08,430
I should behave
because it might reduce my sentence.

259
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:12,268
And from what I can see,
you're the nicest people here.

260
00:14:17,606 --> 00:14:18,649
What do you know?

261
00:14:21,735 --> 00:14:22,778
Nothing.

262
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:26,365
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

263
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:27,408
What do you know?

264
00:14:28,492 --> 00:14:30,035
[STAMMERS] N-Nothing.

265
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:31,495
Is there something I should know?

266
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:38,460
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

267
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:43,340
LoveList was built in the Philippines,

268
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:47,511
but the chase for real connection
is not uniquely Filipino.

269
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:49,555
It's universal.

270
00:14:50,514 --> 00:14:54,226
Our mindset is global
from day one, Mr. Fabrizio.

271
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:56,979
Well, you all know me as a lawyer.

272
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:58,439
I run a firm with my wife,

273
00:14:58,522 --> 00:15:01,400
and on the side, I also invest in tech.

274
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:05,195
Especially, platforms that can be scaled,

275
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:06,822
not just locally,

276
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:08,574
but also internationally.

277
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:12,745
And that's why this
really caught my attention.

278
00:15:12,828 --> 00:15:14,663
You see, my daughter's in her twenties

279
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:17,958
and her entire social life happens
on apps like this.

280
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:21,295
That's why when you sent me the proposal,
it completely made sense.

281
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:24,214
It didn't feel like
just like any other pitch.

282
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:26,383
Of course, we did our due diligence,

283
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:30,554
but from the very start,
I could see its full potential.

284
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:34,016
LoveList was designed
exactly for users like her.

285
00:15:34,099 --> 00:15:36,936
Active, open to real connections,

286
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:38,479
looking for something meaningful.

287
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:39,897
[PETER] Right.

288
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,482
So let's say…
[CLEARS THROAT]

289
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:44,068
…we onboard
three to five million new users

290
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:47,738
within the first six months
after international launching.

291
00:15:48,447 --> 00:15:51,325
How does this affect
your backend architecture?

292
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:56,330
Do you have a projected infrastructure
cost per additional million? Or…?

293
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:59,249
Well, from the start,
it's really built for that.

294
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:00,542
- Right.
- It's based on

295
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:03,253
a cloud system that grows with demand.

296
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:06,757
So we don't have to stop and rebuild

297
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,425
every time there's a traffic spike.

298
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:12,012
Uh, we've run the numbers too.
We know what it takes.

299
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:13,597
- Mm-hmm.
- We're ready.

300
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:15,516
One more question then.

301
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:19,395
Um, what makes LoveList different

302
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:22,022
from all the other swipe apps?

303
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,192
Good question.

304
00:16:25,275 --> 00:16:28,028
Well, LoveList isn't based on swipes.

305
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:31,991
Our matching engine is driven by
how the users behave online.

306
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:35,536
The system tracks how users interact.

307
00:16:35,619 --> 00:16:39,623
We focus on behavior, not just profiles.

308
00:16:39,707 --> 00:16:43,794
How the users talk, engage, respond.

309
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,713
That's where the real signal is.

310
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:49,925
So, over time,
the system gets to know the user,

311
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:53,220
and the quality of matches
improves naturally.

312
00:16:53,762 --> 00:16:55,014
At the end of the day,

313
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:57,933
LoveList isn't just trying
to match people.

314
00:16:58,017 --> 00:17:00,644
We're trying to get to know them more.

315
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:02,479
All right.

316
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:09,486
Well, after reviewing your proposal
and hearing you talk now…

317
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:16,368
I'm in.

318
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:19,038
I can see where this can go.

319
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:20,873
So, let's move forward.

320
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:22,833
I'll have my team coordinate
with the contracts.

321
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:24,168
Okay?

322
00:17:24,251 --> 00:17:26,795
- Great. Great! Thank you.
- All right, thank you.

323
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:28,505
Thank you for the trust, Mr. Fabrizio.

324
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:30,466
Oh, please, just call me Peter.

325
00:17:30,549 --> 00:17:32,134
- Thank you, Peter.
- All right.

326
00:17:32,217 --> 00:17:33,844
- Thank you, Peter.
- Of course.

327
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:36,346
Uh, Peter, can we have a photo with you?

328
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:37,848
Oh, yes. By all means.

329
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:39,641
- [MARJ] Okay. Girls, let's go.
- Let's go.

330
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:41,101
- Here?
- [BILLY] Hey, Morrie.

331
00:17:42,644 --> 00:17:44,563
- Stay in the middle please.
- Oh, all right.

332
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,148
You can take the photo.

333
00:17:48,484 --> 00:17:49,526
[WOMAN] All right.

334
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:52,321
- Smile! One, two, three.
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

335
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:53,363
Another one!

336
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:55,365
- One, two, three.
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

337
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:56,325
- It's done.
- All right.

338
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:57,576
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

339
00:17:57,659 --> 00:17:59,244
Can you now kindly assist Mr. Fabrizio?

340
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,204
All right.

341
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:01,955
- I'll see you guys again.
- Okay, see you.

342
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:02,998
Thank you, sir.

343
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,208
- Take care.
- Thank you.

344
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:12,841
- [SCREAMING, APPLAUDING]
- We closed the deal!

345
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:14,635
- Good job!
- We did it!

346
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:16,470
Oh my God, it's happening!

347
00:18:16,553 --> 00:18:17,888
You guys were amazing.

348
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:22,684
- Shh! He might still be here. Okay, quiet.
- Wait, Billy. Are you really okay now?

349
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:23,936
Are you really okay now?

350
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:25,187
- I'm okay.
- Are you sure?

351
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:26,230
I'm okay.

352
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:30,317
- [DELIGHTED LAUGH, RELIEVED SIGH]
- [OVERLAPPING HAPPY CHATTER]

353
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,777
Wow.

354
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,029
- Wow!
- [TONI] Nice one!

355
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:35,656
- [APPLAUDING]
- Congrats!

356
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:38,158
[INDISTINCT, HAPPY CHATTER
AND GUSHING]

357
00:18:41,036 --> 00:18:43,247
Thanks, Lucy, for all your help.

358
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:47,793
I just hope wherever you end up,
you'll find a job.

359
00:18:48,418 --> 00:18:50,212
Did the principal call you in?

360
00:18:50,879 --> 00:18:52,798
I'm sorry you got dragged into my mess.

361
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:55,092
Dragged into it? Not at all.

362
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:58,303
But yeah, Ma'am Ronquillo talked to me.

363
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:01,723
I denied knowing that Oliver was your son.

364
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,767
But you know, I think

365
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:07,312
if your oldest daughter
talks to the principal,

366
00:19:07,396 --> 00:19:09,231
she might change her mind.

367
00:19:09,314 --> 00:19:10,941
She might reconsider.

368
00:19:11,024 --> 00:19:13,735
I've accepted that Billy won't forgive me.

369
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:15,863
Okay, Billy.

370
00:19:15,946 --> 00:19:18,407
All right, don't worry anymore.
I'll take care of it, okay?

371
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,367
I'll talk to your father.

372
00:19:21,535 --> 00:19:23,745
Just make sure you're sure
about your decision, okay?

373
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:26,623
Okay. Bye, Billy.

374
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:33,714
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

375
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:36,466
[PHONE RINGING]

376
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:41,889
[RINGING CONTINUES]

377
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:46,393
Precious?

378
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:49,062
Enrico, let's meet. We need to talk.

379
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:51,315
Ah, okay, okay.

380
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,984
Where? When?

381
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:56,236
Tonight at seven. Can you make it?

382
00:19:58,238 --> 00:19:59,781
Okay, Enrico. Let's meet.

383
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:05,412
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

384
00:20:12,127 --> 00:20:13,629
<i>I hope you can</i>
<i>forgive me, Precious.</i>

385
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:16,381
<i>I never meant to hurt you.</i>

386
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:19,218
<i>I didn't come here</i>
<i>to listen to your explanation.</i>

387
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:21,762
<i>- But, Pres--</i>
<i>- Listen.</i>

388
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:23,680
<i>You can meet with Oliver.</i>

389
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:26,308
<i>But Billy said I have</i>
<i>to be there too.</i>

390
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:28,352
<i>If it wouldn't have</i>
<i>landed me in prison,</i>

391
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:30,020
<i>I would've killed them!</i>

392
00:20:30,103 --> 00:20:32,773
<i>My husband and his lover!</i>

393
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:35,192
<i>What you're thinking is wrong.</i>
<i>You can't do that.</i>

394
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:38,654
<i>What about having an affair with</i>
<i>a married man? Is that right?</i>

395
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:40,656
<i>Are you sure about</i>
<i>your decision?</i>

396
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:42,115
<i>My brother's all grown up.</i>

397
00:20:42,199 --> 00:20:44,493
<i>I just want to give him the chance</i>

398
00:20:44,576 --> 00:20:46,745
<i>to meet his father,</i>
<i>even just for a little while.</i>

399
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:48,789
<i>I wish I had your courage.</i>

400
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:53,001
[BILLY] <i>You saw how happy</i>
<i>he was earlier, didn't you?</i>

401
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:58,006
<i>Didn't I tell you that decision</i>
<i>was for Oliver?</i>

402
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:05,430
<i>The boss is really in love.</i>

403
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:07,599
- [JORDAN HUMMING]
<i>- He's completely smitten.</i>
